- We want to remove “near me” locations from the search result. For example : when user search for “belfast” it shouldn’t display location that is near the user, should only display location that is the most relevant to the searched term.

- Course Name matching should rank higher then city name match. (Aberdelghy Golf Club should be the first rank course).

Solution:

- Remove the lat/long “must” aggregation from the GeoLocation search query.

- Update PointOfInterest search query to look for

- “must”

- “should” relevant to “Name” and “SearchKey” field, where “SearchKey” only weight 20% to the score.

- apply “near” to the score

Example query :

should: [
{
compound: {
must: [
{
compound : {
should : [
{
autocomplete: {
query: "tpc",
path: "Name",
fuzzy: {
maxEdits: 2,
prefixLength: 3,
maxExpansions: 100
}
}
},
{
autocomplete: {
query: "tpc",
path: "SearchKey",
fuzzy: {
maxEdits: 2,
prefixLength: 3,
maxExpansions: 100
},
score : {
boost : {
value : 0.2
}
}
}
}
]
}
},
{
near: {
origin: {
type: "Point",
coordinates: [
-81.37923, 28.53834
]
},
pivot: 100000.0,
path: "Address.Position"
}
}
]
}
}
]

